  "text": "So I remember when we were talking about doing the daily logs, about doing the energy levels, I'd say I'm probably like a five to four. Didn't get much sleep, woke up kind of tired, napped before work at work. So I got there early. And just kind of remained tired for a lot of the day. Still did well at work, you know, and could shift,\n money, you know. But as far as exploring the emotional aspects of the system, key themes or emotions that I've been experiencing lately, it's kind of tough. I don't really feel\n like there's been any really powerful emotions lately. You know, I'm not disassociating. Mildly, like I was back in like March, April and May. Now that I got more time off, but you know, just putting the nose to the grindstone and doing has to be done. And yeah, just\n wish and I was further along maybe, you know, putting all this work in and feeling like I'm broke paycheck to paycheck kind of sucks. All the reasons I'm putting so much time into the AI stuff is I really want to start paying off. You know, as far as how do I think these might be influencing the good\n systems behavior decision making processes? You know, I don't know if my emotions are necessarily going into the system. I don't really know how that works. Could you elaborate on that too as well?",
